request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> commands  (The failing check was my own guess that `list` hides completed todos by default. The request was only a rename. tsc passes and every existing test passes, so the rename itself looks complete, and forcing a new default could change existing behaviour. I'm replacing the acceptance test so it checks only the rename, and asking the commands owner to make sure no `done` references are left without changing any behaviour.)
round 1: owners commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc exits 0 and all 14 vitest tests pass, including the acceptance test. Todo now has `completed` and no longer has `done`. The acceptance test checks that add and complete set only `completed` and that list still works with completed todos. ListOptions.includeDone is a list option, not the Todo.done field, so I left its name and behaviour unchanged.)

